<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐᾱής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄημι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well ventilated, fresh, airy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρῳ ἐν εὐαεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					599
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐᾰέϊ</span> codd., Rzach).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, of a wind, <i>favourably blowing, fair</i>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσαής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1504
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέμων εὐαέσσιν
			ῥοθίοις</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				773.36
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., <i>favourable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὕπνε . . , εὐαὲς ἡμῖν ἔλθοις</span> [with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				828
			</span></i> (lyr., s.v.l.).</div>
